  "verified": [
    "Visual target parent replacement and field removal, explicit attribute operation, separate destructive-schema and policy acknowledgements, per-asset active owner replacement and mixed-source-version lifecycle mappings.",
    "An invalid owner/state plan returns 422 without changing canonical assets or the type head. Exported plan JSON round-trips; duplicate-key import is rejected through server validation.",
    "A concurrent type publication produces a stale target error. Scope reload preserves an unfinished blank visual owner choice, field operation and draft label without requiring a valid final plan.",
    "An asset added to an existing source-version cohort produces validation failure; always-available scope refresh exposes that new asset for owner repair and preserves other draft choices.",
    "Changing the target while the plan is in JSON mode invalidates old schema/policy acknowledgements; switching back to the visual editor does not reinstate consent.",
    "The complete server preview enumerates all three affected assets with before/after attribute-owner-state tuples. Exact decimal strings survive the transformation.",
    "Concurrent asset mutation invalidates the approved digest: execution returns 409, closes the confirmation dialog and leaves migration state unchanged. Fresh scope review and preview require fresh consent before successful atomic migration.",
    "The immutable receipt survives reload/export/read-back and matches canonical migrated assets. Descendant definitions and their bound assets retain their old exact parent/version pins. Asset audit history links to the typed receipt.",
    "Consumers see no migration ingress and receive 403 for write/context APIs while allowed receipt reads succeed. The foreign tenant receives 404 for the other tenant context/receipt.",
    "All ten existing source/catalog/ownership/audit, model authoring, model migration, inherited type/lifecycle, role/tenant and accessibility journeys pass in the same full twelve-test gate."
  ],
